## Efficient Detection of Test Interference in C Projects (Artifact)

In the four sub-folders, you find the following code and data:

- `scripts`
  Here you find all scripts and tools used. Please see the included `scripts/README.md` for more information

- `data`
  Here you find the base data used in our paper, i.e.:

  - `data/<project>-testsuite-results.csv`
    Base result of the projects testsuite

  - `data/<project>-benchmark-results.csv`
    A list of all benchmark results

  - `data/<project>-coverage-all-runs.csv`
    A list of all coverage results

  - `data/<project>-fd-detected-writes-all.csv`
    A list of all file names which were detected as possibly changed by the FD method

  - `data/<project>-socket-per-test.csv`
    A list of all network sockets used for listening which were detected by the FD method

  - `data/<project>-reduction-per-test.csv`
    A list of all reductions of detected possibly changed files per each test

  - `data/<project>-reduction-per-all-tests.csv`
    A list of all reductions of detected possibly changed files over all tests

  Please refer to `scripts/README.md` for more information.

- `data_analysis`
  Here you find aggregated data from the per-project data in `data` and an analysis script that produces figures and tables from the paper.
  See `data_analysis/README.md` for details.

- `gh_sampling`
  The directory contains the tool we wrote for the multi-stage search for C projects on GitHub that we describe in the paper along with the data we obtained. Please refer to `gh_sampling/README.md` for more details. Please note that this part has only been added *after the artifiact evaluation* during the preparation of our camera-ready version of the paper and has, thus, not been evaluated. 

- The `Dockerfile` in this directory has been used to create the docker image `test_interference_detection-data_mangling.tgz` using this command:
  ```
	docker build -t test_interference_detection/data_mangling -f Dockerfile . 
  ```
  The image can be loaded via 
  ```
  docker load -i test_interference_detection-data_mangling.tgz
  ```
  and run via 
  ```
  docker run --rm -it -v"${PWD}/data_analysis/out":"/data_analysis/out" test_interference_detection-data_mangling
  ```
  This maps the `data_analysis/out` directory from this directory tree into `/data_analysis/out` inside the container, so that tables and figures produced by `data_analysis/analyze_data.R` are written to the host when the script runs inside the container. For details what the script produces from what, please consult `data_analysis/README.md`. To run that script in the pre-configured container (in case you have not already set up R on your host system), use the following commands on the R prompt resulting from the container invocation:
  ```
  setwd("data_analysis")
  source("analyze_data.R")
  ```
</output>
